  "configuration_id": "config_039",
  "reason": "The current best (config_033, acc=0.7131) uses multimodal + multiprofile + scvi_n200 + resnet50 + transformer + weighted. The image modality contributed a meaningful +0.06 boost over RNA-only, but resnet50 is a relatively weak image encoder (0.21 standalone). The most promising unexplored dimension is upgrading the image encoder to imagenet_vit_l, a substantially more powerful pretrained model. config_039 changes only the image encoder (resnet50 → imagenet_vit_l) while keeping all other settings at their proven best values (scvi_n200, multiprofile, transformer aggregation, weighted fusion), isolating the effect of image encoder quality. If a stronger image representation adds more complementary information, this could push past 0.7131. This is the highest-value single-variable extension of the current best, and if it succeeds, experiment 10 can further refine; if it fails, config_033 remains our strong baseline for the final experiment."
}

